meta {
  name: Place an order
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/orders
  body: json
}

body:json {
  {
    "fulfilment": {
      "1": "pickup"
    },
    "user_address_id": null,
    "accept_terms": true
  }
}

docs {
  Takes **no money**. Payment is a separate step, so an order exists to come
  back to even if the buyer's data runs out at the wrong moment.

  Writes an order per shop inside one order group, snapshots the monetisation
  policy and the escrow windows onto each order, records a `TermsAcceptance`
  naming every policy version, and empties the cart.

  Throttled to ten a minute — the most expensive thing a buyer can ask for.
}
